   "text": {
    "L1": "Multiplication with integers has two parts: find the number, then find its sign.",
    "L2": "Three times negative two means three jumps of two to the left from zero, landing at negative six.",
    "L3": "Now look at the pattern: the products rise by two as the first factor drops by one.",
    "L4": "After zero times negative two is zero, the next product is positive two.",
    "L5": "So a negative times a negative gives a positive product, such as negative three times negative four equals twelve.",
    "L6": "Different signs give a negative product. With several factors, an even number of negatives is positive and an odd number is negative.",
    "L7": "Remember, two negatives make a positive in multiplication and division, not in addition."
   },
